135	  <h1>ADC Transfer Functions: the Reference as the Unit of Measure</h1>
136	  <p class="tagline">Why this matters: an ADC code is not a voltage — it is a ratio against the selected reference. Until commit 58b7e2d the MSP430 model hardcoded 3.3 V, so every reference-scaling bug in user code was invisible to SIL tests.</p>
137	</header>
