286	    {l:'VREF2.0 → 2.0 V; VREF2.5 → 2.5 V (REF_A outputs)',t:['2.0','2.5','ref_a','internal']},
287	    {l:'VEREF → _veref_v, external VeREF+ pin, settable via 2nd param',t:['veref','external','pin','_veref_v','second param','2.1']}],
288	 m:`VALID_ADC_REFERENCES = frozenset({"AVCC", "VEREF"} | set(ADC_INTERNAL_REF_V)) — six tokens:
289	- AVCC → whatever CPU:VCC currently is (read live from clock.vcc; default 3.3 V). Models the analog supply rail.
290	- VREF → 1.2 V. Bare VREF maps to REFVSEL's reset value (00b = 1.2 V) in REF_A.
291	- VREF1.2 → 1.2 V, VREF2.0 → 2.0 V, VREF2.5 → 2.5 V. REF_A's three internal bandgap-derived outputs (SLAU367P §33.3.1).
292	- VEREF → self._veref_v (default 1.2 V; reset by *RST). Models the external VeREF+ pin; the board-supplied voltage is settable with a second parameter, e.g. ADC:REFERENCE VEREF,2.1.
293	Anything else has no ADC12VRSEL encoding → ScpiError -224.`
294	},
