321	{id:'r4',ch:'refs',type:'w',
322	 q:'Explain the two-parameter form ADC:REFERENCE VEREF,2.1 — what each parameter does, what happens if the second parameter is "notanumber", and what *RST does to this state.',
323	 c:[{l:'param 1 selects the external VeREF+ pin as VR+',t:['veref','external','pin','vr+','select']},
324	    {l:'param 2 sets the board-supplied pin voltage (_veref_v = 2.1)',t:['_veref_v','2.1','board','voltage','second param','float']},
325	    {l:'non-numeric → ScpiError -104 Data type error',t:['-104','data type','valueerror','notanumber']},
326	    {l:'*RST resets _veref_v to 1.2',t:['*rst','reset','1.2']}],
327	 m:`Parameter 1 (VEREF) selects the external VeREF+ pin as the VR+ source — _adc_reference_voltage() then returns self._veref_v at conversion time.
328	Parameter 2 (2.1) sets the pin's voltage: the handler does self._veref_v = float(cmd.params[1]). This exists because VeREF+ is board-supplied (SLASE54D Table 7-1 — no defined reset state after BOR); the test declares what the board wires up.
329	If the second parameter is "notanumber", float() raises ValueError and the handler converts it to ScpiError(-104, "Invalid VEREF voltage: notanumber") — a data-type error, distinct from -224 (illegal value). test_veref_voltage_param_must_be_numeric pins this: one queued error, no crash.
330	*RST resets _veref_v to 1.2 along with the rest of the peripheral state, so the two-parameter form must be re-sent after any reset.`
331	},
