358	{id:'c2',ch:'code',type:'w',
359	 q:'Walk through _adc_reference_voltage() added in 58b7e2d: how is VR+ resolved for each reference kind, why does it read self.adc[0].reference, and what does the model deliberately NOT expose?',
360	 snip:`<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">_adc_reference_voltage</span>(self) -> float:
361	    ref = self.adc[<span class="num">0</span>].reference
362	    <span class="kw">if</span> ref == <span class="str">"AVCC"</span>:
363	        <span class="kw">return</span> self.clock.vcc
364	    <span class="kw">if</span> ref == <span class="str">"VEREF"</span>:
365	        <span class="kw">return</span> self._veref_v
366	    <span class="kw">return</span> ADC_INTERNAL_REF_V.get(ref, self.clock.vcc)`,
367	 c:[{l:'AVCC → clock.vcc read live at conversion time',t:['clock.vcc','live','cpu:vcc','supply']},
368	    {l:'VEREF → _veref_v (external pin state)',t:['_veref_v','veref','external','pin']},
369	    {l:'else → ADC_INTERNAL_REF_V lookup (REF_A 1.2/2.0/2.5)',t:['adc_internal_ref_v','dict','lookup','1.2','2.0','2.5']},
370	    {l:'adc[0] because _adc_ref sets ALL channels to one reference',t:['adc[0]','all channels','single','one reference','every channel']},
371	    {l:'VR− half of ADC12VRSEL not exposed (fixed AVSS 0 V)',t:['vr−','vr-','avss','not expose','0 v','fixed']}],
372	 m:`Three branches:
373	1. AVCC → returns self.clock.vcc, read live at every conversion. CPU:VCC 3.0 immediately rescales the next RAW read — the supply IS the reference.
374	2. VEREF → returns self._veref_v, the externally supplied VeREF+ pin voltage set via ADC:REFERENCE VEREF,<v>.
375	3. Anything else → ADC_INTERNAL_REF_V.get(ref, self.clock.vcc): REF_A's internal outputs (VREF/VREF1.2 → 1.2, VREF2.0 → 2.0, VREF2.5 → 2.5), with clock.vcc as a defensive fallback.
376	It reads self.adc[0].reference because the model keeps a single device-wide reference: the _adc_ref setter loops over all channels ("for ch in self.adc.values(): ch.reference = ref"), so channel 0 is representative of all of them.
377	The docstring states the deliberate limitation: VR− is fixed at AVSS (0 V). Real ADC12VRSEL encodings also choose the VR− source; the simulator only models which source drives VR+.`
378	},
