482	  {t:'≈1.21 V — raw is 1861 because the simulator still encodes against 3.3 V',c:false,w:'int(1.5/3.3×4095) = 1861 was the OLD encoding. After 58b7e2d the simulator honours VREF2.5, so raw = 2457.'},
483	  {t:'The code is correct — 3.3 is the required constant for a 3.3-V supply part',c:false,w:'The supply is irrelevant to decoding; the selected REFERENCE defines the code\'s unit. With VREF2.5 selected, 3.3f is simply the wrong constant.'},
